  "rationale": "Bobby Hutcherson's second Blue Note leader date is an exemplary mid-1960s Blue Note session pairing a stellar sextet (Freddie Hubbard, James Spaulding, Herbie Hancock, Ron Carter, Joe Chambers) with a bold two-sided concept: Hutcherson's hard-bop compositions on side one, Chambers' avant-tinged pieces on side two. AllMusic 5 stars, Penguin Guide 3.5 stars. 'Little B's Poem' is a Hutcherson classic. The session gravity alone—five of the six musicians are already in this canon as leaders—makes it a load-bearing record of the post-bop era.",
